meta {
  name: Space Register Notify
  type: http
  seq: 160
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.registerNotify
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://{{did}}/space/org.example.bucket/main",
    "service": "did:web:syncer.example.com#atproto_space_syncer"
  }
}

docs {
  Subscribe a service to write notifications for every repo in a space. The subscriber is named
  by a service identifier — a DID with an optional "#fragment" naming the DID-document entry to
  deliver to — rather than a URL, because notifyWrite is delivered with service auth addressed
  to that identifier. The identifier is resolved at registration, so a typo is reported here
  (400 ServiceNotResolvable) instead of producing a subscription that never delivers.

  Returns "expiresAt": registrations lapse, and re-registering renews. Notification is
  best-effort — a syncer that misses one heals from the commit hash on its next listRepoOps, or
  from a listRepos sweep — so a delivery failure never unregisters the subscriber.

  Answered only by the space's authority (400 SpaceNotFound otherwise). Auth: a space
  credential, or the authority's own session.
}
